// Title: Github Self-Hosted Runner Execution
// Sigma ID: 5bac7a56-da88-4c27-922e-c81e113b20cb
// Status: test | Level: medium
// Author: Daniel Koifman (KoifSec)
// Date: 2025-11-29 | Modified: -
// ATT&CK: command-and-control, T1102.002, T1071
// Description: Detects GitHub self-hosted runners executing workflows on local infrastructure that could be
//   abused for persistence and code execution. Shai-Hulud is an npm supply chain worm targeting
//   CI/CD environments. It installs runners on compromised systems to maintain access after
//   credential theft, leveraging their access to secrets and internal networks.
// False positives:
//   - Legitimate GitHub self-hosted runner installations on designated CI/CD infrastructure
//   - Authorized runner deployments by DevOps/Platform teams following change management
//   - Scheduled runner updates or reconfigurations on existing build agents
//   - Self-hosted runners that follow expected/known naming patterns
//   - Installation via expected/known configuration management tools (reflected mostly as parent process name)
// References:
//   - https://about.gitlab.com/blog/gitlab-discovers-widespread-npm-supply-chain-attack/
//   - https://securitylabs.datadoghq.com/articles/shai-hulud-2.0-npm-worm/
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/ccbb0369507f796db0b0ae6854c8a2be471b9d84/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_github_self_hosted_runner.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where ((FolderPath endswith "\\Runner.Worker.exe" or ProcessVersionInfoOriginalFileName =~ "Runner.Worker.dll") and ProcessCommandLine contains "spawnclient") or ((FolderPath endswith "\\Runner.Listener.exe" or ProcessVersionInfoOriginalFileName =~ "Runner.Listener.dll") and (ProcessCommandLine contains "run" or ProcessCommandLine contains "configure"))
